cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Quantifying AI Risk: a telemetry-driven risk scoring engine for production AI"
message: "If you use this software or the methodology, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Modekurty
    given-names: Suneeta
    affiliation: SANJEEVANI AI
    website: "https://www.linkedin.com/in/smodekurty"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sanjeevaniai/quantifying-ai-risk"
url: "https://github.com/sanjeevaniai/quantifying-ai-risk"
abstract: >
  An educational reference implementation of a telemetry-driven governance
  measurement pipeline for production AI systems: decision-bound governance
  telemetry, measurement contracts that declare every reported quantity before it
  is computed, a typed evidence model that refuses to let control evidence update a
  system-behaviour posterior, per-measure Bayesian state estimation with credible
  intervals and an INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE state, a Monte Carlo risk model that keeps
  frequency and consequence separate, and machine-readable decision contracts a
  CI/CD pipeline can gate on. Companion repository to an O'Reilly live training
  course.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI risk
  - telemetry
  - observability
  - Bayesian inference
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - MLOps
  - model risk management
  - measurement
